  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "## CreditCardDetails Updated for New TryCreate Pattern\n\n### Breaking Changes\n- **CreditCardDetails.TryCreate**: Now accepts nullable parameters (`string?` for card number and security number, `int?` for expiration month and year) to better handle incomplete data.\n- Method signature updated to support scenarios where credit card information may not be fully provided (e.g., form submissions, builder patterns).\n\n### Improvements\n- **Comprehensive Validation**: All validation errors are now collected and returned together, providing complete feedback about all issues in a single call.\n- **Better Error Handling**: Validates all fields even when some are missing, returning detailed error messages for each invalid field.\n- **Consistent Error Codes**: All validation errors include error codes (\"Required\", \"InvalidMonth\", \"Expired\", etc.) for better programmatic error handling.\n- **Builder Pattern Support**: CreditCardBuilder now fully leverages the updated TryCreate method with nullable parameters.\n\n### Other Domain Models\nDomain models including Address, ContactInformation, PersonName, and CreditCardDetails with their respective builders.",
